We need to build complete retrosynthesis route JSON using given data. We have template ID 1914385 and its mapped_rxn. Also we have precursors list from applying template: [['C=CC=C', 'COC(=O)C1=CC(=O)C1']]. So target molecule? Not directly given. The route should be root molecule with smiles? We need target SMILES. Not provided. Maybe the target is the product of the reaction defined by mapped_rxn. The mapped_rxn string includes product on right side after >>. The product SMILES is after >>: "[CH3:1][O:2][C:3](=[O:4])[C@:5]12[CH2:6][CH:7]=[CH:8][CH2:9][C@H:10]1[C:11](=[O:12])[CH2:13]2". That's the target molecule. So route: root mol with that SMILES, children reaction with template_id 1914385, children precursors mols: "C=CC=C" and "COC(=O)C1=CC(=O)C1". Need to ensure type fields. So JSON:

{
 "type":"mol",
 "smiles":"[CH3:1][O:2][C:3](=[O:4])[C@:5]12[CH2:6][CH:7]=[CH:8][CH2:9][C@H:10]1[C:11](=[O:12])[CH2:13]2",
 "children":[
   {
     "type":"reaction",
     "template_id":1914385,
     "children":[
       {"type":"mol","smiles":"C=CC=C"},
       {"type":"mol","smiles":"COC(=O)C1=CC(=O)C1"}
     ]
   }
 ]
}

We should verify route schema using verify_route. Let's call tool.
